  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Formulation Mission Green Growth Greenland</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Green Growth is the second priority area of the Greenland MIP, with the overall goal to sustainably support Greenland&apos;s economic diversification and with specific targets on renewable energy, biodiversity and research coordination (but not limited to these sectors). The identification mission&apos;s purpose is to identify how to best support these goals - which implementations modalities, which targets, which policies - and to support the drafting of the relevant programming documents (annual action plan, action document, financing agreement). Key experts will undertake undertake research, interviews, reporting and drafting to that end.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
